Za, the roaming gnome (Ran-Gno-Neu), has had a tough life, or series
of lives rather.  He'd succumbed to nearly all the early YASDs (spiked
poisoned pit, orc with the wand of striking, team a, etc.) before
finally becoming nearly ascendable.  With half the kit assembled and a
WoW(1:3) in hand, he then proceeded to sacrifice himself by meleeing
when he should have run away (or at least missiled).  Rats... but on
the very next attempt, the RNG showed something that seems
astonishingly like pity.

DL2 houses a general store.  Faithful Max the dog trots through the
contents, retrieving a Hawaiian shirt.  Wear-testing reveals it to be
+4 - bonus!  But I'm not wearing a rare shirt until I can be safe from
poly traps.  Max trots off and brings back a pair of unIDed cloaks.
Having displacement already, I try them on.  The first is protection,
but the second doesn't self ID.  A little chill runs down the spine,
memories of a past life perhaps; I don the shirt.  Max also fetches a
few other handy items, including several scrolls, potions, and a
wooden flute.  In finding the downstair, I find a bag, but alas it is
some form of sack.

On arriving at DL3, there's a non-matching bag sitting near the
stairs. The bag is not tricks, and with a random statue I discover
that it is indeed a bag of holding.  DL3 has two other nice features,
a co-aligned altar and another general store.  Max does his duty
again, bringing me the one amulet and a number of scrolls and
potions.  Putting on the amulet reveals nothing, but I price ID some
scrolls and find identify.  Max also retrieves a couple of uncursed
clear potions.  I make up some holy water and ID the amulet as
reflection!  Now with half an ascension kit at DL3, it's time to start
some serious planning--I wish I was skilled enough to try for a speed
run, but I've yet to ascend a Ranger so I'll be patient.  First order
of business is poison resistance to avoid another unfortunate YASD, so
I turn aside from the gnome-friendly confines of the Mines.  Sokoban
is fortunately close at DL6, and a random guardian naga hatchling
(peaceful or not) provides the requisite intrinsic.

Now it's time to go find that luckstone... though it seems like I
already have it...



